ex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:a5c1132f0feb886ae000028d409270f8c504e26a74899f71a4e5c12b40161c3e","file":"preprints/Integral-and-fractional-expectation-thresholds-are-equivalent-September-23-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex","line":52,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"3262209e3590cb4593660f59c2ae1538e44e1a37dd9d1054762f75b8fbab2703","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Integral-and-fractional-expectation-thresholds-are-equivalent-September-23-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:a5c1132f0feb886ae000028d409270f8c504e26a74899f71a4e5c12b40161c3e","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Integral-and-fractional-expectation-thresholds-are-equivalent-September-23-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex#L52"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every finite nonempty $X$ and every nonempty proper increasing\nfamily $\\F\\subseteq2^X$,\n\\[\n q_f(\\F)\\le25\\cdot512^4\\,q(\\F).\n\\]\nBoth thresholds use the budget $1/2$. The constant is independent of\n$|X|$, the sizes of the minimal members of $\\F$, and the support of\nthe fractional cover."}
